---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import VerdictBox from '../components/VerdictBox.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
import { breadcrumbs } from '../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
  { name: 'Privacy', path: '/privacy/' },
];

const updated = '2026-09-01';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What ShopOwnerStack collects, what happens to a demo request, what analytics we run and how to get your data removed."
  path="/privacy/"
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbs(crumbs)]}
>
  <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />

  <div class="wrap pt-8">
    <h1 class="font-condensed text-5xl font-bold uppercase leading-none sm:text-6xl">Privacy</h1>

    <VerdictBox class="mt-6" label="The short answer">
      <p>
        We collect what you type into a form and anonymous analytics about which pages get read.
        Demo request details go to the vendor named on that form and nowhere else. We do not sell
        anything to anyone.
      </p>
    </VerdictBox>

    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-muted">
      Last updated <time datetime={updated}>1 September 2026</time>.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="wrap-narrow prose-shop mt-12">
    <h2>What we collect</h2>

    <p>Three things, and nothing else:</p>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Form submissions.</strong> If you submit a demo request we collect your name,
        business name, email, phone, trade and team size, plus which product the request was for.
        If you subscribe to the newsletter we collect your email address.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Analytics.</strong> Anonymous, aggregated page view data via Google Analytics 4,
        including which outbound partner links are clicked and from which page. We do not attempt
        to identify individual visitors.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Server logs.</strong> Our host records standard request logs, including IP
        addresses, for security and abuse prevention.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What happens to a demo request</h2>

    <p>
      The details you enter are passed to the vendor named on that form so they can contact you
      about a demo. That vendor then holds your details under their own privacy policy, and you
      should read it if that matters to you.
    </p>

    <p>
      We keep a copy so we can tell whether a referral worked. We do not pass demo request details
      to any vendor other than the one on the form, and we do not add you to our mailing list
      because you asked for a demo.
    </p>

    <h2>Newsletter</h2>

    <p>
      If you subscribe, we use your email address to send occasional updates when a score changes
      or a price moves. Every email has a one-click unsubscribe, and unsubscribing removes your
      address rather than suppressing it.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>

    <p>
      We use Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages are read and which partner links are
      clicked. That sets cookies in your browser. If you block them, the site works exactly the
      same - nothing on this site depends on analytics loading.
    </p>

    <p>
      Partner links may set a cookie on the vendor's side so they can attribute a referral. That
      is the vendor's cookie under the vendor's policy, and it is why every outbound link is
      marked as sponsored before you click it.
    </p>

    <h2>What we do not do</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>Sell, rent or trade your details</li>
      <li>Pass demo request details to vendors you did not ask about</li>
      <li>Run advertising trackers or retargeting pixels</li>
      <li>Ask for payment details - we never take money from readers</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your data, on request</h2>

    <p>
      Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a> and ask for a copy of what we hold
      about you, or ask us to delete it. We will do either within 30 days. If you have asked a
      vendor for a demo, you will need to ask that vendor separately for their copy.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>

    <p>
      If this page changes materially, the date at the top changes with it. {SITE.name} is
      operated from the address given on the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
